The Fifth Prosperous Empire of the Sundom (Sundom, for short) was an empire of hundreds of vassal states, spread across the majority of an arm of the [[Geography/index|Astra]]. The empire was founded out of the ruins of the Fourth Sundom, with the single goal of the total annihilation of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]]. The Sundom's magic number is three.

While it was unsuccessful in achieving its goal, the many, desperate, attempts made to create weaponry capable of killing a Thessian litter the Astra. These remnants are often pivotal to the power struggles between the fractured vassals of the fallen empire in the political vacuum it left.

[[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] is one of those experiments. The empire set its [[Phenomena/Althane/Cycle|cycle]] turning to raise a mortal strong enough to kill a Thessian, seeding it with volunteers who went to sleep for the work and reincarnate with each turn of the wheel. Their memories were to be given back only to one who passed the trial: broke [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]] and escaped [[Divinity/Immix|the Lighthouse]] alive. The empire that began this is long dead, and the sleepers it left behind live as the people of the world, most of them never knowing what they were. Some among them now mean to wake the rest, end the cycle, and finish the war the Sundom could not.

One of its experimental stealth bombers, made to fight the Thessians, crashed in the [[Geography/Ushas/Far Realms|Far Realms of Ushas]]. Its crew's descendants lived on in the wreck, regressed and ignorant of their origin, and one of the original crew, the [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] [[People/Althane/SeRaan|SeRaan]], lay deactivated there; the Kaathe were one of the empire's original member species. [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] grew out of that wreck.

Its magic is built on looms: a clear-titanium shell holding a rotating disc that spools thread around itself when filled with magic, until the thread, charged enough, snaps and unleashes the effect. The Sundom kept a tuning ritual that could match the weave of a world to its own, so that any sphere that joined might mingle with the rest without either weave unravelling. The knowledge of it is lost; it would have to be taken from one of the old Sundom worlds.

The Sundom built stations and ships run by minds of its own making, kept for tasks too complex for people, such as running a ship or an orbital platform; they were held to be people like any other and could leave their posts in walking platforms. Some of those old stations, such as the third Sundom's [[Geography/Inevitable Everdawn/index|Inevitable Everdawn]], still drift in the Astra, dark and cold, sunk into the edge of [[Phenomena/The Slip|the slip]].
